4. schema read out of `information_schema` -> `beforeMigration`;
5. the current deploy's migration applied through the REAL `migrateWithBackup` with `requestId === CURRENT_COMMAND` — the durable join — which DUMPS BEFORE IT APPLIES. `backupRef` asserted non-null;
6. a FURTHER out-of-band mutation (`CREATE TABLE mutated_after_migration`), so "the schema came back" cannot be satisfied by a rollback that did nothing;
7. `deployment.rollback` with `restoreDatabase: true` through the registered handler and the REAL `nodeBackupPorts` (no injected port);
